(ServiceHub Backend: What Is in Place) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In one sentence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This is the starter structure for the ServiceHub backend. A scaffold is the foundation of a) Tj
T*
(project: it gives later features a place to go, but it does not mean those features have) Tj
T*
(been built.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What works today) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The server starts with `npm run dev`.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/health` responds with `{ "status": "ok" }`.) Tj
T*
(- One automated test checks that health response.) Tj
T*
(- `npm test` and `npm run lint` both pass.) Tj
T*
(- Environment settings are checked with Zod when the app starts.) Tj
T*
(- Requests are logged, common security headers are set, CORS and JSON parsing are) Tj
T*
(configured, and API requests are rate limited.) Tj
T*
(- Errors go through one handler and use a consistent JSON shape: `{ "error": { "code":) Tj
T*
("...", "message": "..." } }`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(How the folders are organized) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `src/app.js` assembles Express middleware and routes. `src/server.js` starts the listening) Tj
T*
(server.) Tj
T*
(- `src/config/` validates settings. `src/middlewares/` contains request handling stubs and) Tj
T*
(middleware.) Tj
T*
(- `src/modules/` groups code by feature. The planned modules are auth, users, businesses,) Tj
T*
(services, staff, schedules, appointments, reviews, notifications, dashboard, audit logs, and) Tj
T*
(platform admin. Each has routes, controller, service, repository, and validation placeholder) Tj
T*
(files.) Tj
T*
(- `src/database/` contains the Prisma client setup and a transaction helper.) Tj
T*
(`prisma/schema.prisma` defines PostgreSQL as the database provider but has no business) Tj
T*
(models yet.) Tj
T*
(- `src/lib/`, `src/jobs/`, and `src/realtime/` hold placeholders for logging, Redis/BullMQ) Tj
T*
(jobs, and Socket.IO.) Tj
T*
(- `tests/` contains the health endpoint test. `docs/` describes architecture, API) Tj
T*
(conventions, and tenancy guidance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What is not built yet) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Authentication, business and user features, appointment flows, database models, real Redis) Tj
T*
(connections, job workers, and Socket.IO events are not implemented. The auth,) Tj
T*
(tenant-context, RBAC, and validation middleware files currently pass requests through; they) Tj
T*
(do not secure routes yet. The health endpoint is the only implemented route.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tenant design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The documented plan is one shared PostgreSQL database. Future tenant-owned tables should) Tj
T*
(include `businessId`; tenant repositories should include that ID in every relevant query.) Tj
T*
(Tenant context should come from an authenticated business membership. This is design) Tj
T*
(guidance only until the models and middleware are implemented.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
